From 65b5a92450ece0795384054d7c5fe37530569a03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:53:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(settings): connect a Mastodon account for automated
 posts

Part of opencollective/opencollective#7138. Adds an "Automated posts"
settings section where collectives, funds, projects, events and
organizations connect a Mastodon account (server URL + access token)
and choose which posts are published: thanks to new financial
contributors, contributor milestones and monthly stats.

- Each connected account can be toggled per post type or disconnected.
  Accounts whose token was revoked show a warning and can be
  reconnected with a new token.
- The section is behind the MASTODON_POSTS preview feature (closed beta
  for platform accounts, enabled in development), matching the
  MICROBLOGGING_POSTS feature flag on the API.
- Schema and generated types updated for the new API fields
  (ConnectedAccountService.mastodon, instanceUrl,
  editConnectedAccountPostSettings, ConnectedAccount.username).
